md`*Default state, as first seen with typical data. Say what is on screen and what each control does when pressed.*`
// %%
artboard_empty = svgLens({ keyboard: true })`<svg viewBox="0 0 640 360" width="100%" style="max-width:640px;background:#f6f7f9" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif">
  <rect x="16" y="16" width="608" height="328" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#c9ced6"/>
  <rect x="16" y="16" width="608" height="44" rx="6" fill="#eef0f4" stroke="#c9ced6"/>
  <text x="32" y="44" font-size="15" fill="#1f2933">Title</text>
  <text x="320" y="190" font-size="14" fill="#52606d" text-anchor="middle">Nothing here yet</text>
  <rect x="260" y="210" width="120" height="36" rx="5" fill="#2f6bff"/>
  <text x="320" y="233" font-size="13" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">Add the first</text>
</svg>`
// %%
md`*Empty state: no data yet. Add a drawing for each further state by copying a drawing cell and renaming it \`artboard_<state>\`, then list it below.*`
// %%
states = [
  { state: "default", drawing: "artboard_default", when: "data present" },
  { state: "empty", drawing: "artboard_empty", when: "no data yet" },
  { state: "loading", drawing: null, when: "…" },
  { state: "error", drawing: null, when: "…" }
]
// %%
statesTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th>state</th><th>when</th><th>drawing</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${states.map((s) => htl.html`<tr data-state=${s.state}><td>${s.state}</td><td>${s.when}</td><td>${s.drawing ? htl.html`<code>${s.drawing}</code>` : htl.html`<em>not drawn</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
// %%
md`### Visual constraints

*What the drawings cannot say: the theme variables to use for colour, the narrowest width it must work at and what reflows there, which existing component each control is.*`
// %%
md`## Behaviour

One requirement per row, in priority order: if time runs out, the bottom rows go first. \`check\` is how anyone can tell the row holds, as a command, a test name, or a thing to do and see.`
// %%
requirements = [
  { id: "R1", text: "When <trigger>, the <thing> shall <response>.", check: "<command, test name, or action and what is seen>" },
  { id: "R2", text: "While <state>, the <thing> shall <response>.", check: "" }
]
// %%
requirementsTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th>id</th><th>requirement</th><th>check</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${requirements.map((r) => htl.html`<tr data-requirement=${r.id}><td><strong>${r.id}</strong></td><td>${r.text}</td><td>${r.check ? htl.html`<code>${r.check}</code>` : htl.html`<em>none</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
// %%
md`### Worked examples

*Real inputs and the outputs they must produce, as cells. Where the logic is small enough, write it here and let the notebook run it: a running example cannot disagree with itself, and the cells become the implementation's first tests.*`
// %%
examples = [
  { given: "<input>", expect: "<output>" }
]
// %%
md`## Design

*How it is built, at the level of parts and what passes between them. Diagrams first, then the decisions. The two below are mermaid text: press **edit** on one to change it. Keep the flowchart for what the parts are and the sequence for the order things happen in; delete whichever the work does not need. \`stateDiagram-v2\` and \`erDiagram\` work the same way. Mermaid loads from a CDN, so these two cells need a network connection.*`
// %%
architecture = onPaper(mermaid`flowchart LR
  input[input] --> part[the new part]
  part --> output[output]
  part -. reads .-> store[(existing store)]`)
// %%
sequence = onPaper(mermaid`sequenceDiagram
  participant U as User
  participant P as the new part
  participant S as existing store
  U->>P: action
  P->>S: read
  S-->>P: rows
  P-->>U: result`)
// %%
md`### Decisions

*Each decision already made, with the alternative that was rejected and what it would have cost. The implementer does not reopen these.*

| decided | instead of | because |
|---|---|---|
| *…* | *…* | *…* |

### Known traps

*What looks like the obvious approach and does not work, with the evidence.*`
// %%
md`## Handover

### Where the work goes

*Files and modules to change, by path. The existing code to copy the pattern from, by path and name. Documents to read first.*

### Boundaries

| | |
|---|---|
| **always** | *run the checks below before reporting done* |
| **ask first** | *adding a dependency; changing a shared module* |
| **never** | *…* |

### Checks

*The exact commands, and what passing looks like. The implementer reports their output, not a claim that they pass.*

\`\`\`
…
\`\`\`

### Steps

*Ordered. Mark where to stop and show the result before going on.*

1. *…*
2. *…* **stop and show**`
// %%
md`## Open questions

A question marked blocking stops the handover. Each open one is listed in the strip at the top with a link to its row here. One decision per row: if an answer leaves part of the question undecided, that part is a new row, not a sentence inside the answer.`
// %%
questions = [
  { q: "<question>", blocking: true, answer: "" }
]
// %%
questionsTable = htl.html`<table style="font-size:.9em">
  <thead><tr><th></th><th>question</th><th>answer</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>${questions.map((q, i) => htl.html`<tr data-question=${i}><td>${q.blocking && !q.answer ? "blocking" : ""}</td><td>${q.q}</td><td>${q.answer || htl.html`<em>open</em>`}</td></tr>`)}</tbody>
</table>`
// %%
// mermaid draws dark text on no background, which is unreadable on a dark theme.
onPaper = (node) => htl.html`<div style="max-width:640px;background:#f6f7f9;border-radius:6px;padding:10px">${node}</div>`
// %%
specModule = "__SPEC_MODULE__"
